  <data name="Calibration_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Calibrate fans</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Calibration_Step1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Measures the speed of each fan from 100% down to 20%.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Calibration_Step2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• If a fan stops at low power, finds out how much it needs to spin again and keeps it above that.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Calibration_Step3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Saves a reference: LinkFlow warns you when a fan starts spinning well below normal (dust or a worn bearing).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Calibration_Duration" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>It takes about 2 minutes: the hub changes the speed gradually. The fans ramp up to full speed and then slow down. Avoid games and heavy tasks meanwhile. If the CPU, the GPU or the coolant reaches its alert temperature, the calibration stops and the fans go back to the profile.</value>
